<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Necho II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 610–595 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Pharaoh Necho II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Necho II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s Twenty-sixth Dynasty in the late seventh and early sixth centuries BCE. He intervened in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> in support of the collapsing Assyrian state. His defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carchemish">Battle of Carchemish</a> in 605 BCE secured the Levant for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/necho-ii.jpg" alt="Necho II" width="172" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Keith Schengili-Roberts · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Necho-KnellingStatue_BrooklynMuseum.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Battle of Carchemish in 605 BCE, won by the crown prince Nebuchadnezzar II against the Egyptian army of <b>Pharaoh Necho II</b>, secured the Levant and turned a regional kingdom into the dominant power of the ancient Near East.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 609 BCE Josiah was killed at Megiddo confronting the pharaoh <b>Necho II</b>, who then installed Jehoiakim as his vassal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Herodotus tells how Phoenician sailors sent by the pharaoh <b>Necho II</b> sailed round Africa in three years.</blockquote><a href="/culture/phoenicians">Phoenicians · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Necho II</b> began a canal from the Nile to the Red Sea, sent a Phoenician fleet around Africa and killed King Josiah of Judah at Megiddo, but lost to Babylon at Carchemish in 605 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/twenty-sixth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-sixth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li></ul></section>
